+# Build validation — S5-CLM-00003492
+
+The validation basis is an offline, clean-output Lean replay from the
+task-local worktree.  A fresh output tree (`/tmp/s5_3492_cold_final7.g7aovm`)
+was used; the transient systemd service allowed only `AF_UNIX`, while the
+pinned dependency oleans were read from the canonical Lean environment.
+Target modules were rebuilt from the exact claim-owned sources.
+
+```text
+systemd-run --user --quiet --pipe --wait --collect \
+  -p RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_UNIX \
+  env LEAN_PATH=<pinned-library-roots> lean --trust=0 \
+  -R <claim-work>/Formalizations/Lean -o <cold-root>/.../Statement.olean \
+  <claim-work>/.../Statement.lean
+# Repeat the same wrapper for Proof.lean and Audit.lean.
+systemd-run --user --quiet --pipe --wait --collect \
+  -p RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_UNIX /usr/bin/python3 -I -B -c pass
+```
+
+All Lean processes run with network-disabled policy and exit zero.  The rebuilt
+oleans are Statement 20496 bytes (`d748c46d90dd…`), Proof 299600 bytes
+(`e23e1a81ba97…`), and Audit 2776 bytes (`f711ddd87c22…`).  The audit
+output has the expected `#check` declarations and exact foundation census.
+The prescribed claim self-check exits zero.  JSON strictness, artifact hashes,
+proof-DAG acyclicity, anchor injectivity/reverse coverage, forbidden-token
+scanning, exact owned-path coverage, and adversarial mutations are checked by
+the task-local package audit.
+
+Exact argv digests, times, stream hashes, rebuilt read traces, artifact hashes,
+and mutation results are sealed in `receipts/current-validation.json`.  The
+receipt is provisional until the canonical Master repeats validation against
+integrated bytes.
